{
 "source": "Paired 20,000-update training runs (scripts/validate): per-arm values parsed from the fairseq logs and the held-out evaluations by analyze.py; the criterion as computed by verdict.py.",
 "recipe": "The measured recipe (8 Hopper GPUs, yoco_3b, bf16, --zero-sharding os, lr 1.5e-4 with 50 warm-up updates and polynomial decay over 300,000) with --max-update 20000 and --seed 1 or 2; production mode (no deterministic algorithms); 20,000 updates = 328M tokens (0.8 fineweb-edu, 0.2 codeparrot), less than one pass over either training file. Model-only bf16 checkpoints every 2,000 updates.",
 "heldout": "First 3,000 documents of fineweb-edu sample/10BT/001_00000.parquet (training used 000_00000) and the first 800 of codeparrot-clean file-000000000002.json.gz (training used file 1), same dataset revisions; 4 fineweb documents whose exact text occurs in the training shards dropped. Packed like the training loader: 800 fineweb samples (1,638,400 tokens) and 200 code samples (409,600 tokens) of 2,048 targets. Loss = fp32 next-token cross-entropy in bits, evaluated with the reference model code for every arm; mix = 0.8 fineweb + 0.2 code.",
 "train_loss": "fairseq training loss (bits per token), mean of the ten logged 10-update values in each block of 100 updates; train_loss_bits_per100[i] covers updates 100*i+1 .. 100*(i+1).",
 "hosts": "A and B are two hosts of the same model (eight 80 GB Hopper GPUs each). opt_s2 ran on host B in parallel with ref_s2; its time per update is not compared.",
 "criterion": "Y = ref_s2 - ref (seed-to-seed yardstick); E1 = opt - ref; E2 = opt_s2 - ref_s2; S = opt_s2 - opt. Consistent at a checkpoint if |E1|, |E2| and |S| are each <= |Y|. Training-loss rows use the mean of the 1,000 updates up to the checkpoint. Defined before the two seed-2 arms had finished and not changed afterwards.",
